    "subtopicId": "systems-two-linear-equations",
    "subtopic": "Systems of two linear equations in two variables",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "stem": "<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">If <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the ordered pair x comma y \"></span></span> is the solution to the given system of equations, what is the value of <span class=\"italic\">y</span> ?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": "23.",
    "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is 23. Since it&rsquo;s given that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 2\"></span>, the value of <span class=\"italic\">y</span> can be found by substituting 2 for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the first equation and solving for <span class=\"italic\">y</span>. Substituting 2 for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 times 2, plus y, equals 29\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"6 plus y, equals 29\"></span>. Subtracting 6 from both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals 23\"></span>.</p>",
    "passage": "<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Equation 1: 3 x plus y, equals 29. Equation 2: x equals 2\"></span></span></p></div>"
